config BR2_PACKAGE_VIRGILIO_BASE
	bool "virgilio-base"
	depends on BR2_USE_MMU # procd/netifd fork()
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBUBOX
	select BR2_PACKAGE_UBUS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_UCI
	select BR2_PACKAGE_PROCD
	select BR2_PACKAGE_UBOX
	select BR2_PACKAGE_NETIFD
	select BR2_PACKAGE_JSONFILTER
	help
	  Generic base system shared by every Virgilio device (the OpenWrt
	  "base-files" role), independent of board, SoC and application
	  packages:

	   - procd init scripts + rc.d layout (boot, network, system, ...)
	   - /etc/config/system default
	   - system glue: lib/functions*.sh, rc.common, ifup/ifdown/ifstatus,
	     service, hotplug-call, login.sh, inittab, preinit
	   - profile, motd, hotplug dispatch config

	  Application service wiring (init scripts, uci defaults, tools)
	  ships with the app packages: camilladsp-genconf + init/config in
	  camilladsp, ptp-monitor + init/config in statime, uci defaults in
	  inferno. Their uci defaults are overridable per device via the
	  board rootfs overlay (applied after all packages).

	  Selects the uci/procd stack it requires (procd pulls ubus and
	  udebug, netifd pulls json-c/libnl/ucode). Device-specific files
	  (network topology, ALSA config, FIR coefficients, board fixups,
	  test-rig services) stay in the per-board rootfs overlay.
